{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UptC3SuRy3BDA4sSQZKynJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the project and the experiment plan. I need to identify the \"planned\" (status: planned or orphaned) experiments and generate detailed predicted data for the \"worst\" tier.\n\nThe planned/orphaned experiments are:\n1. exp-017 (planned) - ner_llama_conll\n2. exp-019 (planned) - simple_verifier_baseline\n3. exp-020 (orphaned) - fewnerd_smoke\n4. exp-021 (orphaned) - fewnerd_full\n5. exp-022 (orphaned) - 3rd_seed_scierc\n\n\n6. exp-023 (orphaned) - lora_rank8_ablation\n7. exp-024 (planned) - claim_audit\n\nThough I'm noticing exp-017 is marked as planned in the CLAUDE.md file, but the registry shows its tasks are already completed, so there's some inconsistency between the plan status and actual execution state.\n\nLooking back at the experiment_plan.yaml, it only defines experiments exp-012 through exp-024 without status fields — those come from the CLAUDE.md context instead. Scanning through the statuses there, most experiments from exp-001 through exp-017 show DONE, except exp-003 which is orphaned, and exp-017 which is listed as planned despite having completed registry entries.\n\nThe remaining experiments that need predicted data are exp-017, exp-019, exp-020, exp-021, exp-022, exp-023, and exp-024 — though exp-017 appears to have actually been completed based on the registry, so I should verify the experiment_plan data more carefully to determine which ones truly still need work.\n\nLooking at the definitions of the worst tier, I need to understand what makes an experiment qualify: Few-NERD cases with unusual patterns like high F1 scores paired with low degeneracy that breaks the typical relationship, plus instances where at least one signal significantly outperforms the greedy baseline.\n\nI'm also considering the LoRA rank=8 results where degenera