ulations. The Few-NERD worst tier shows 5.3% degeneracy despite higher F1 than SciERC, which breaks the expected monotonic pattern, and LoRA rank=8 drops to 5.2% from 21% at rank=16—a 15.8 percentage point delta. Since I'm being internally consistent with the definition, I can move forward with generating the final output.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39245,"cache_read_input_tokens":79110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39245},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6745f76e-d74d-4b80-8f31-9d576877709a","uuid":"318a2055-ce1f-45a8-8743-bdcc98fcef7a"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WzVKugKPm1M6a6fBP7nYwP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the data needed to produce calibrated predictions. Here's the comprehensive worst-tier prediction for all planned/orphaned experiments:\n\n```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  放弃 capability trap 作为 unifying framework。Reframe 为条件性研究：\n  'Conditions for Effective Test-Time Scaling in Structured IE'。\n  核心转向：不是 'selection universally fails'，而是 'selection fails under\n  high-convergence regimes induced by aggressive fine-tuning, but succeeds\n  when output diversity is preserved.'\n  LP compression 仍成立（free-form ablation 证据不受影响）。\n  Instance degeneracy 从 'inevitable consequence of capability' 变为\n  'controllable artifact of training configuration'。\n  Paper 变 prescriptive：给出什么条件下可以/不可以用 multi-sample 策略。\n  标题改为 'When Does Multi-Sample Selection Help Structured IE?\n  A Diagnostic Study of Output Convergence'。\n  仍冲 EMNLP Main——从 novel insight paper 转为 large-scale empirical study\n  with actionable guidelines。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-020: Few-NERD Smoke Test\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-020: fewnerd_smoke\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-020\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD INTRA (coarse 8-type) smoke test: 1-epoch LoRA fine-tune\n      on Qwen3-8B + N=8 pilot inference on 200 instances.\n      验证数据管线和模型可学性，Gate exp-021.\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 200\n      n_valid: 188\n      n_gold_empty: 12\n      parse_rate: 0.985\n      parse_failures: 24\n      N: 8\n      T: 1.0\n      seed: 42\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.718\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.828\n      ner_headroom_pp: 11.0\n      degeneracy_rate: 0.101\n      sj_rho_full: 0.192\n      fk_rho_full: 0.148\n      lp_rho_full: 0.214\n      vc_rho_full: 0.248\n      em_rho_full: 0.175\n      sj_auroc: 0.582\n      lp_auroc: 0.604\n      vc_auroc: 0.638\n      em_auroc: 0.621\n      lp_selection_f1: 0.740\n      lp_selection_delta_pp: 2.2\n      greedy_selection_ref: 0.718\n      sample_f1_pct_zero: 5.3\n      sample_f1_mean: 0.671\n      sample_f1_std: 0.248\n      fleiss_kappa_mean: 0.371\n      soft_jaccard_mean: 0.612\n      elapsed_minutes: 18\n      train_loss_1epoch: 0.142\n      eval_loss_1epoch: 0.128\n    result_rationale: >\n      1-epoch fine-tune 不够充分训练，F1=0.718 低于 full run 预期（~0.78）\n      但已验证任务可学性。Degeneracy 10.1% 初步暗示 Few-NERD 不符合\n      capability trap 预测——按 capability trap 的 F1→degeneracy 单调关系，\n      0.718 F1 应对应 ~15-20% degeneracy（介于 SciERC 21% 和 WNUT 0% 之间），\n      但实际更低。原因：(a) Few-NERD 每句平均 3-4 实体、多词实体边界变异空间大；\n      (b) 1-epoch 训练保留了预训练模型的高输出多样性，weight update 幅度小；\n      (c) coarse 8-type 标签系统清晰，类型错误少但边界变异多。\n      SJ rho 仅 0.192 因 inter-sample 结构一致性弱——不同样本在多词实体\n      边界上产生变化，SJ 对此敏感但 F1 对此宽容。\n      LP rho 0.214 略优于 SJ，初步提示 LP 在低 degeneracy regime 下有效。\n      LP selection +2.2pp 是 directional positive，200 instances 样本量\n      不足以达到统计显著但方向明确。Smoke test 通过，gate exp-021.\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S-smoke: Few-NERD Smoke Test QE Metrics (n=188, 1-epoch, N=8)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"rho_full\", \"AUROC\", \"tau\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"VC\", 0.248, 0.638, 0.180]\n          - [\"LP\", 0.214, 0.604, 0.153]\n          - [\"SJ\", 0.192, 0.582, 0.139]\n          - [\"EM\", 0.175, 0.621, 0.125]\n          - [\"FK\", 0.148, 0.555, 0.108]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Bar chart: degeneracy rate at smoke test stage across datasets\n        (Few-NERD 10.1% vs SciERC 21% vs CoNLL 58% vs WNUT ~0%).\n        Few-NERD 已经偏低于 capability trap 预测线.\n    analysis: >\n      Smoke test 成功验证数据管线和模型训练。关键早期信号：\n      degeneracy rate (10.1%) 明显低于 capability trap 对 F1=0.718 的预测值 (~15-20%),\n      暗示 fine-tuning 配置（1 epoch, LoRA rank=16）而非 capability 驱动 degeneracy。\n      LP 在 QE 和 selection 上均优于 SJ，与 SciERC 模式不同——\n      提示数据集特性对最优信号有影响。Gate 通过，进入 exp-021 full run。\n      注意 parse_rate 0.985 可接受，fine-tuned model 对 Few-NERD 格式适应良好。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-021: Few-NERD Full (KEY EXPERIMENT)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-021: fewnerd_full\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-021\"\n    description: >\n      Few-NERD INTRA (coarse 8-type) full experiment: 3-epoch LoRA fine-tune +\n      N=8 inference on full test set with 3 seeds [42, 123, 456].\n      Captures log-probs. 第三个 NER 数据集，Main Conference 必要条件.\n    expected_results:\n      # Dataset metadata\n      n_instances_total: 5218\n      n_valid: 4506\n      n_gold_empty: 712\n      N: 8\n      T: 1.0\n      lora_rank: 16\n      lora_alpha: 32\n      epochs: 3\n      # Training\n      train_final_loss: 0.058\n      eval_loss: 0.072\n      train_runtime_min: 95\n      # Per-seed NER results\n      seed42_ner:\n        greedy_f1: 0.782\n        oracle_f1: 0.873\n        headroom_pp: 9.1\n        degeneracy_rate: 0.048\n        sj_rho_full: 0.238\n        fk_rho_full: 0.183\n        lp_rho_full: 0.291\n        vc_rho_full: 0.312\n        em_rho_full: 0.228\n        sj_auroc: 0.624\n        fk_auroc: 0.588\n        lp_auroc: 0.658\n        vc_auroc: 0.681\n        em_auroc: 0.718\n        sj_tau: 0.172\n        lp_tau: 0.211\n        lp_selection_f1: 0.818\n        vc_selection_f1: 0.805\n        sj_selection_f1: 0.798\n        fk_selection_f1: 0.793\n        em_selection_f1: 0.795\n        random_f1: 0.769\n        sample_f1_pct_zero: 3.8\n        tied_fraction_f1: 0.048\n        lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.088\n      seed123_ner:\n        greedy_f1: 0.776\n        oracle_f1: 0.868\n        headroom_pp: 9.2\n        degeneracy_rate: 0.055\n        sj_rho_full: 0.208\n        fk_rho_full: 0.165\n        lp_rho_full: 0.271\n        vc_rho_full: 0.285\n        em_rho_full: 0.210\n        lp_selection_f1: 0.808\n        vc_selection_f1: 0.798\n        sj_selection_f1: 0.791\n        random_f1: 0.764\n        sample_f1_pct_zero: 4.1\n        lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.083\n      seed456_ner:\n        greedy_f1: 0.775\n        oracle_f1: 0.865\n        headroom_pp: 9.0\n        degeneracy_rate: 0.058\n        sj_rho_full: 0.203\n        fk_rho_full: 0.170\n        lp_rho_full: 0.262\n        vc_rho_full: 0.289\n        em_rho_full: 0.198\n        lp_selection_f1: 0.805\n        vc_selection_f1: 0.796\n        sj_selection_f1: 0.789\n        random_f1: 0.762\n        sample_f1_pct_zero: 4.5\n        lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.081\n      # 3-seed aggregation\n      mean_greedy_f1: 0.778\n      mean_oracle_f1: 0.869\n      mean_headroom_pp: 9.1\n      mean_degeneracy_rate: 0.054\n      sd_degeneracy_rate: 0.005\n      mean_sj_rho_full: 0.216\n      sd_sj_rho_full: 0.019\n      mean_fk_rho_full: 0.173\n      sd_fk_rho_full: 0.009\n      mean_lp_rho_full: 0.275\n      sd_lp_rho_full: 0.015\n      mean_vc_rho_full: 0.295\n      sd_vc_rho_full: 0.015\n      mean_em_rho_full: 0.212\n      sd_em_rho_full: 0.015\n      # Selection aggregation\n      mean_lp_selection_f1: 0.810\n      mean_lp_selection_gap_pp: 3.2\n      lp_selection_bootstrap_ci95: [0.004, 0.060]\n      lp_selection_bootstrap_p: 0.028\n      lp_selection_cohen_d: 0.152\n      mean_vc_selection_gap_pp: 2.1\n      vc_selection_bootstrap_p: 0.065\n      mean_sj_selection_gap_pp: 1.5\n      sj_selection_bootstrap_p: 0.12\n      # LP compression comparison\n      mean_lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.084\n      lp_range_ratio_vs_scierc: 2.05\n      # Capability trap update\n      capability_trap_r2_3datasets: 0.98\n      capability_trap_r2_4datasets_with_fewnerd: 0.51\n      capability_trap_regression_residual_fewnerd_pp: 30.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Few-NERD 打破 capability trap 的 F1→degeneracy 单调预测：\n      F1=0.778（高于 SciERC 0.664）但 degeneracy 仅 5.4%\n      （远低于 SciERC 21%，更远低于 CoNLL 58%）。\n      按 capability trap 线性回归，F1=0.778 应预测 ~35-40% degeneracy。\n      实际偏差超过 30pp。\n\n      低 degeneracy 的根因：\n      (1) 实体密度高——Few-NERD INTRA 每实例平均 3.4 个实体（vs SciERC 2.1），\n      更多实体意味着更多的组合变异空间。即使每个实体的 type 高度一致\n      （coarse 8-type 系统下类型错误极少），多词实体的边界变异\n      仍能产生不同的 entity sets——不同的 sets 有不同的 F1。\n      (2) 3-epoch LoRA（vs SciERC 5-epoch）对预训练权重修改幅度更小，\n      输出分布未被压缩至 mode collapse。\n      (3) 8 类粗粒度标签意味着类型空间简单，\n      模型不需要 overly specialize 就能达到高 F1，保留了 generation diversity。\n\n      Selection 首次显著有效：LP +3.2pp (p=0.028, d=0.152)。\n      这是全研究中首个某信号显著优于 greedy 的结果。\n      LP 成功的原因：degeneracy 低 → LP 有真实 within-instance variance\n      (median range 0.084 nats, 是 SciERC 0.041 的 2×) → LP 可区分好坏样本。\n      VC +2.1pp 接近显著 (p=0.065)。SJ +1.5pp 不显著 (p=0.12)——\n      SJ 的弱 rho (0.216) 限制了其 selection 能力。\n\n      SJ rho 仅 0.216 的原因：coarse entity types 使得 SJ 的\n      type-aware matching 在多数实例上给出高分（类型一致），\n      区分力来自边界差异——但边界差异与 F1 的对齐度弱。\n      LP 直接捕获 generation confidence，与 F1 的关联更强。\n      这是与 SciERC 的关键区别：SciERC 上 SJ > LP (rho 0.36 vs 0.21)，\n      Few-NERD 上 LP > SJ (rho 0.275 vs 0.216)。\n      信号有效性取决于数据集特性，不存在 universal best signal。\n\n      Capability trap R² 从 0.98 (3 datasets) 降至 0.51 (4 datasets)。\n      Few-NERD 是一个明确的 outlier，残差 30.2pp。\n      这迫使叙事从 \"capability drives degeneracy\" 转向\n      \"fine-tuning intensity and dataset properties drive degeneracy\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Few-NERD QE Metrics (3-seed mean +/- SD, N=8, T=1.0, n=4506)\"\n        columns: [\"Signal\", \"rho_full\", \"SD\", \"AUROC\", \"tau\", \"Sel_F1\", \"Delta_greedy_pp\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LP\", 0.275, 0.015, 0.658, 0.211, 0.810, \"+3.2\", \"0.028*\"]\n          - [\"VC\", 0.295, 0.015, 0.681, 0.214, 0.799, \"+2.1\", \"0.065\"]\n          - [\"SJ\", 0.216, 0.019, 0.624, 0.172, 0.793, \"+1.5\", \"0.12\"]\n          - [\"EM\", 0.212, 0.015, 0.718, 0.153, 0.793, \"+1.5\", \"0.13\"]\n          - [\"FK\", 0.173, 0.009, 0.588, 0.125, 0.790, \"+1.2\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"greedy\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", 0.778, \"---\", \"---\"]\n          - [\"oracle\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", 0.869, \"+9.1\", \"---\"]\n          - [\"random\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", \"---\", 0.765, \"-1.3\", \"---\"]\n      - name: \"Table 6: Capability Trap — F1 vs Degeneracy Across 4 Datasets\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"greedy_F1\", \"degen_pct\", \"predicted_degen_pct\", \"residual_pp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CoNLL-2003\", 0.912, 58.0, \"55-60\", \"~0\"]\n          - [\"Few-NERD*\", 0.778, 5.4, \"35-40\", \"-30.2\"]\n          - [\"SciERC\", 0.664, 21.0, \"20-25\", \"~0\"]\n          - [\"WNUT-17\", 0.523, 0.0, \"0-5\", \"~0\"]\n      - name: \"Table 7: LP Compression Comparison Across Datasets\"\n        columns: [\"Dataset\", \"LP_range_median_nats\", \"degen_pct\", \"LP_sel_gap_pp\", \"LP_sel_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Few-NERD\", 0.084, 5.4, \"+3.2\", 0.028]\n          - [\"SciERC NER\", 0.041, 21.0, \"+0.6\", 0.39]\n          - [\"CoNLL NER\", 0.018, 58.0, \"-1.0\", 0.62]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 4 (CRITICAL): Scatter plot — greedy F1 (x) vs degeneracy rate (y)\n        for 4 datasets + 4B data point. Regression line from CoNLL/SciERC/WNUT\n        (R²=0.98, dashed). Few-NERD plotted as red triangle, massive residual visible.\n        Annotated R² drop (0.98 → 0.51). Shows capability trap breakdown.\n      - >\n        Figure 5: Selection F1 vs N curves for Few-NERD (N=1,2,4,8).\n        LP line rises monotonically above greedy baseline (horizontal dashed).\n        Contrast panel: SciERC curves are flat. Demonstrates recovered TTS scaling.\n      - >\n        Figure 6: LP within-instance range distributions — three overlaid histograms\n        for Few-NERD (median 0.084), SciERC (0.041), CoNLL (0.018).\n        Few-NERD distribution visibly shifted right, showing reduced LP compression.\n    analysis: >\n      Few-NERD 实验产生三个核心 worst-tier 结论：\n\n      (1) Capability trap 预测失败 (R² 0.98→0.51)。F1=0.778 + degen=5.4%\n      不在 F1→degeneracy 回归线上。Few-NERD 的残差 30.2pp 是压倒性的\n      反面证据。\"Capability drives degeneracy\" 被替换为\n      \"degeneracy is a joint function of fine-tuning intensity,\n      entity density, and task structure.\"\n\n      (2) Selection 在低 degeneracy regime 下有效。LP +3.2pp (p=0.028)\n      证明 \"universal failure\" 不成立。Selection 失败是 condition-dependent,\n      not structural. 关键条件：degeneracy < 10% + LP range > 0.08 nats.\n\n      (3) 最优信号依赖数据集。SciERC: SJ > LP. Few-NERD: LP > SJ.\n      不存在 universal best signal——进一步支持 conditional/prescriptive framing.\n      Paper 需要给出 practitioners 决策指南：根据数据集的 degeneracy rate\n      和 LP compression degree 选择策略 (multi-sample vs greedy).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-022: 3rd Seed SciERC (KEY EXPERIMENT)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-022: 3rd_seed_scierc\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-022\"\n    description: >\n      SciERC NER+RE N=8 第三个 seed (seed=789).\n      强化 Fisher p-value power，测试 cross-seed stability.\n    expected_results:\n      n_instances: 551\n      n_valid_ner: 529\n      n_valid_re: 397\n      N: 8\n      T: 1.0\n      seed: 789\n      parse_rate: 1.0\n      # NER results\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.658\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.772\n      ner_headroom_pp: 11.4\n      ner_degeneracy_rate: 0.235\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.285\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.218\n      ner_lp_rho_full: 0.228\n      ner_vc_rho_full: 0.338\n      ner_em_rho_full: 0.272\n      ner_sj_rho_cond: 0.248\n      ner_fk_rho_cond: 0.162\n      ner_lp_rho_cond: 0.178\n      ner_vc_rho_cond: 0.295\n      ner_em_rho_cond: 0.345\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.648\n      ner_fk_auroc: 0.598\n      ner_lp_auroc: 0.578\n      ner_vc_auroc: 0.662\n      ner_em_auroc: 0.738\n      ner_lp_selection_f1: 0.650\n      ner_sj_selection_f1: 0.645\n      ner_greedy_ref: 0.658\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 13.2\n      # RE results\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.412\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.582\n      re_headroom_pp: 17.0\n      re_sj_rho_full: 0.308\n      re_fk_rho_full: 0.248\n      re_lp_rho_full: 0.192\n      re_vc_rho_full: 0.293\n      re_em_rho_full: 0.198\n      re_sj_rho_cond: 0.352\n      re_lp_rho_cond: 0.022\n      re_zero_f1_pct: 44.8\n      # 3-seed NER aggregation (seed42=0.360, seed123=0.385, seed789=0.285)\n      three_seed_ner_sj_rho_values: [0.360, 0.385, 0.285]\n      three_seed_ner_sj_rho_mean: 0.343\n      three_seed_ner_sj_rho_sd: 0.053\n      three_seed_ner_fk_rho_values: [0.267, 0.290, 0.218]\n      three_seed_ner_fk_rho_mean: 0.258\n      three_seed_ner_fk_rho_sd: 0.037\n      three_seed_ner_lp_rho_values: [0.205, 0.225, 0.228]\n      three_seed_ner_lp_rho_mean: 0.219\n      three_seed_ner_lp_rho_sd: 0.013\n      three_seed_ner_vc_rho_values: [0.379, 0.395, 0.338]\n      three_seed_ner_vc_rho_mean: 0.371\n      three_seed_ner_vc_rho_sd: 0.030\n      # 3-seed RE aggregation\n      three_seed_re_sj_rho_values: [0.250, 0.283, 0.308]\n      three_seed_re_sj_rho_mean: 0.280\n      three_seed_re_sj_rho_sd: 0.029\n      three_seed_re_fk_rho_values: [0.275, 0.317, 0.248]\n      three_seed_re_fk_rho_mean: 0.280\n      three_seed_re_fk_rho_sd: 0.035\n      three_seed_re_lp_rho_values: [0.266, 0.290, 0.192]\n      three_seed_re_lp_rho_mean: 0.249\n      three_seed_re_lp_rho_sd: 0.051\n      three_seed_re_vc_rho_values: [0.350, 0.320, 0.293]\n      three_seed_re_vc_rho_mean: 0.321\n      three_seed_re_vc_rho_sd: 0.029\n      # RE ranking per seed (worst tier: inconsistent)\n      re_ranking_seed42: \"VC(0.350) > FK(0.275) > LP(0.266) > SJ(0.250) > EM(0.134)\"\n      re_ranking_seed123: \"FK(0.317) > LP(0.290) > SJ(0.283) > VC(0.320) > EM(0.170)\"\n      re_ranking_seed789: \"SJ(0.308) > VC(0.293) > FK(0.248) > EM(0.198) > LP(0.192)\"\n      re_ranking_top1_consistent: false\n      # Fisher combined p-values\n      fisher_sj_gt_lp_ner_individual_p: [0.002, 0.003, 0.180]\n      fisher_sj_gt_lp_ner_combined_p: 0.085\n      fisher_sj_gt_fk_ner_combined_p: 0.032\n      fisher_vc_gt_lp_ner_combined_p: 0.018\n      fisher_structural_gt_surface_ner_combined_p: 0.042\n      # Coefficient of variation\n      ner_sj_cv: 0.154\n      ner_lp_cv: 0.059\n      re_sj_cv: 0.104\n      re_lp_cv: 0.205\n    result_rationale: >\n      Seed 789 暴露 NER SJ rho 的 seed-to-seed 不稳定性。\n      SJ rho=0.285 是三个 seed 中最低值，显著低于 seed42 (0.360)\n      和 seed123 (0.385)。3-seed SD=0.053 在定义范围 [0.04, 0.07] 内。\n\n      低 SJ rho 的来源：seed 789 的随机采样在 medium-difficulty 实例\n      (greedy F1 0.4-0.7) 上产生了与其他 seed 不同的输出分布——\n      这些实例中模型产生了多样但质量差异小的输出，\n      SJ 无法从结构一致性中区分好坏。SJ 对 sampling randomness\n      的敏感度高于 LP (CV 0.154 vs 0.059)，因 SJ 是 pairwise comparison\n      的平均值，对极端样本敏感。LP 是每个样本的独立属性，\n      受 sampling 影响更小。\n\n      RE 信号排名跨 seed 完全不一致是最重要的发现：\n      - seed42: VC 最强 → seed123: FK 最强 → seed789: SJ 最强。\n      三个不同的 top-1 signal. 这说明 RE 上 n=397 + 44.8% zero-F1\n      使得任何无监督信号的排名都不稳定。单 seed RE 结论不可信。\n      Cross-seed 一致的唯一结论：EM 始终最弱 (0.134/0.170/0.198)。\n\n      Fisher combined p=0.085 对 SJ>LP (NER) 的含义：\n      seed42 (p=0.002) 和 seed123 (p=0.003) 给出强证据，\n      但 seed789 (p=0.180) 大幅削弱了 combined evidence。\n      使用 Meng's test（考虑 SJ-LP 间 Pearson r≈0.55），\n      seed789 的 SJ-LP gap 仅 0.057 (0.285-0.228)，\n      在 n=529 下不够显著。Fisher 将三个 p-values 合并后\n      给出 borderline result。\n\n      VC>LP (p=0.018) 仍显著——structural family 作为整体\n      优于 surface signals 的结论可用 VC 作为 anchor，\n      但 SJ 的优势变得 seed-dependent。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: SciERC NER 3-Seed QE (N=8, T=1.0, n=529)\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"SJ_rho\", \"FK_rho\", \"LP_rho\", \"VC_rho\", \"EM_rho\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, 0.360, 0.267, 0.205, 0.379, 0.295]\n          - [123, 0.385, 0.290, 0.225, 0.395, 0.310]\n          - [789, 0.285, 0.218, 0.228, 0.338, 0.272]\n          - [\"mean\", 0.343, 0.258, 0.219, 0.371, 0.292]\n          - [\"SD\", 0.053, 0.037, 0.013, 0.030, 0.020]\n          - [\"CV\", 0.154, 0.143, 0.059, 0.081, 0.068]\n      - name: \"Table 9: SciERC RE 3-Seed Signal Rankings\"\n        columns: [\"Seed\", \"Rank_1\", \"Rank_2\", \"Rank_3\", \"Rank_4\", \"Rank_5\"]\n        rows:\n          - [42, \"VC(0.350)\", \"FK(0.275)\", \"LP(0.266)\", \"SJ(0.250)\", \"EM(0.134)\"]\n          - [123, \"VC(0.320)\", \"FK(0.317)\", \"LP(0.290)\", \"SJ(0.283)\", \"EM(0.170)\"]\n          - [789, \"SJ(0.308)\", \"VC(0.293)\", \"FK(0.248)\", \"EM(0.198)\", \"LP(0.192)\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: Fisher Combined P-values (3-seed NER)\"\n        columns: [\"Comparison\", \"p_s42\", \"p_s123\", \"p_s789\", \"Fisher_p\", \"Conclusion\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SJ > LP\", 0.002, 0.003, 0.180, 0.085, \"borderline (alpha=0.10)\"]\n          - [\"SJ > FK\", 0.005, 0.004, 0.120, 0.032, \"significant (alpha=0.05)\"]\n          - [\"VC > LP\", 0.001, 0.001, 0.038, 0.018, \"significant (alpha=0.05)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 7: Error bar plot — NER signal rho across 3 seeds.\n        SJ shows widest error bars (SD=0.053). LP shows narrowest (SD=0.013).\n        Seed 789 SJ (0.285) is a clear low outlier, nearly overlapping with LP.\n      - >\n        Figure 8: Heatmap — RE signal ranking by seed (3x5 grid).\n        Color intensity = rank position. Visual chaos demonstrates\n        complete ranking inconsistency.\n    analysis: >\n      3rd seed 暴露两个关键弱点：\n\n      (1) NER SJ rho instability (SD=0.053, CV=0.154): 2-seed 分析低估真实变异。\n      Seed 789 的 SJ rho=0.285 接近 LP (0.228)，SJ 的优势 seed-dependent。\n      Fisher combined p=0.085 意味着 SJ>LP 在 alpha=0.05 下不显著。\n      论文应用 VC (p=0.018) 作为 structural>surface 的 primary evidence，\n      SJ 降为 complementary signal。\n\n      (2) RE 信号排名跨 seed 不一致: 无 reliable winner。\n      RE 结论限定为 \"no unsupervised signal reliably ranks RE quality;\n      all signals are weak and unstable under cross-seed variation.\"\n      这不是 failure of analysis——这是 genuine empirical finding，\n      strengthens the conditional framing: \"reliability depends on\n      task structure and sample size.\"\n\n      对 worst tier 叙事的影响: SJ instability + RE ranking chaos\n      进一步削弱 universal claims，支持 conditional/prescriptive pivot。\n      NER 上 signal effectiveness 有 regime dependency (dataset × seed)，\n      RE 上所有 unsupervised signals 都不可靠。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-023: LoRA Rank=8 Ablation (KEY EXPERIMENT)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-023: lora_rank8_ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-023\"\n    description: >\n      LoRA rank=8 ablation on SciERC: fine-tune with rank=8\n      (vs baseline rank=16) + N=8 inference.\n      测试 fine-tuning intensity 是否是 degeneracy 的主驱动.\n    expected_results:\n      # Training config\n      base_model: \"Qwen3-8B\"\n      lora_rank: 8\n      lora_alpha: 16\n      lora_dropout: 0.0\n      epochs: 5\n      dataset: \"SciERC\"\n      train_final_loss: 0.108\n      eval_loss: 0.115\n      best_checkpoint: \"checkpoint-400\"\n      train_runtime_min: 24\n      # Inference config\n      N: 8\n      T: 1.0\n      seed: 42\n      n_valid_ner: 529\n      n_valid_re: 397\n      parse_rate: 1.0\n      # NER results\n      ner_greedy_f1: 0.625\n      ner_oracle_f1: 0.812\n      ner_headroom_pp: 18.7\n      ner_degeneracy_rate: 0.052\n      ner_degeneracy_delta_vs_rank16_pp: -15.8\n      ner_sj_rho_full: 0.378\n      ner_fk_rho_full: 0.288\n      ner_lp_rho_full: 0.252\n      ner_vc_rho_full: 0.408\n      ner_em_rho_full: 0.312\n      ner_sj_rho_cond: 0.362\n      ner_fk_rho_cond: 0.258\n      ner_lp_rho_cond: 0.218\n      ner_sj_auroc: 0.698\n      ner_fk_auroc: 0.645\n      ner_lp_auroc: 0.622\n      ner_vc_auroc: 0.712\n      ner_em_auroc: 0.758\n      ner_sj_ece: 0.408\n      ner_lp_ece: 0.652\n      ner_em_ece: 0.318\n      # NER selection\n      ner_lp_selection_f1: 0.661\n      ner_sj_selection_f1: 0.653\n      ner_vc_selection_f1: 0.648\n      ner_fk_selection_f1: 0.645\n      ner_em_selection_f1: 0.642\n      ner_random_f1: 0.598\n      ner_greedy_ref: 0.625\n      ner_oracle_ref: 0.812\n      ner_lp_selection_gap_pp: 3.6\n      ner_lp_selection_bootstrap_p: 0.015\n      ner_lp_selection_cohen_d: 0.168\n      ner_lp_selection_ci95: [0.008, 0.064]\n      ner_sj_selection_gap_pp: 2.8\n      ner_sj_selection_bootstrap_p: 0.042\n      # LP compression\n      ner_lp_within_instance_range_median: 0.074\n      ner_lp_within_instance_std_mean: 0.032\n      ner_tied_fraction_f1: 0.052\n      ner_sample_f1_pct_zero: 15.8\n      ner_sample_f1_mean: 0.545\n      ner_sample_f1_std: 0.312\n      # RE results\n      re_greedy_f1: 0.388\n      re_oracle_f1: 0.598\n      re_headroom_pp: 21.0\n      re_degeneracy_rate: 0.12\n      re_degeneracy_delta_vs_rank16_pp: -9.0\n      re_sj_rho_full: 0.238\n      re_fk_rho_full: 0.342\n      re_lp_rho_full: 0.288\n      re_vc_rho_full: 0.318\n      re_em_rho_full: 0.185\n      re_zero_f1_pct: 48.5\n      re_lp_rho_cond: 0.115\n      re_lp_rho_cond_p: 0.078\n      re_lp_selection_f1: 0.415\n      re_lp_selection_gap_pp: 2.7\n      re_lp_selection_p: 0.068\n      # Comparison with rank=16 baseline\n      comparison_rank16_ner_f1: 0.664\n      comparison_rank8_ner_f1: 0.625\n      comparison_f1_delta_pp: -3.9\n      comparison_rank16_degeneracy: 0.210\n      comparison_rank8_degeneracy: 0.052\n      comparison_degeneracy_delta_pp: -15.8\n      comparison_rank16_oracle_headroom: 10.85\n      comparison_rank8_oracle_headroom: 18.7\n      comparison_headroom_gain_pp: 7.85\n      comparison_rank16_lp_range_median: 0.041\n      comparison_rank8_lp_range_median: 0.074\n      comparison_lp_range_ratio: 1.80\n      comparison_rank16_sj_rho: 0.360\n      comparison_rank8_sj_rho: 0.378\n      comparison_sj_rho_delta: 0.018\n      comparison_rank16_lp_sel_gap_pp: 0.6\n      comparison_rank8_lp_sel_gap_pp: 3.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      LoRA rank=8 ablation 是 worst tier 的因果证据核心。\n\n      F1 下降有限 (-3.9pp: 0.664→0.625)。rank=8 的参数空间更小\n      (rank-8 矩阵 vs rank-16), 模型学到了 SciERC NER 的主要 extraction\n      patterns 但未达到 rank=16 的精度。5 epochs 同样训练量下，\n      rank=8 的有效 capacity 更低，final loss 0.108 vs rank=16 的 0.081。\n      但 0.625 F1 仍然是 reasonable performance（高于 WNUT 0.523）。\n\n      Degeneracy 大幅下降 15.8pp (21%→5.2%)。这是最关键的发现。\n      机制：rank=8 LoRA 对预训练权重的修改幅度更小。\n      预训练 Qwen3-8B 的 generation distribution 是 diverse 的；\n      fine-tuning 将这个 distribution 压缩向 task-specific modes。\n      Rank=16 提供了足够的 capacity 来 aggressively specialize\n      (更多参数 → 更大的 weight update → 更强的 mode collapse)。\n      Rank=8 参数不足以完全 collapse output distribution，保留了多样性。\n\n      Oracle headroom 从 10.85pp 增加到 18.7pp (+7.85pp)。\n      更多的输出多样性意味着 N=8 samples 覆盖更广的 output space,\n      oracle 能找到更好的 sample。这直接转化为 selection 机会：\n      LP selection +3.6pp (p=0.015, d=0.168)。\n\n      LP compression 显著减轻：median range 0.074 vs 0.041 (1.80×)。\n      更宽的 LP range → LP 有更多的 discrimination power →\n      selection 从 negligible (+0.6pp, n.s.) 变为 significant (+3.6pp, p=0.015)。\n\n      SJ rho 在 rank=8 下甚至略高 (0.378 vs 0.360, +0.018)。\n      这证明 QE correlation 能力不受 fine-tuning intensity 影响——\n      signals 的 quality estimation 能力是 robust 的。\n      只有 selection 受 degeneracy/compression 影响。\n      这 disentangles QE vs selection：QE 是 signal 的 intrinsic property，\n      selection effectiveness 是 regime-dependent。\n\n      RE degeneracy 也下降但幅度更小 (-9.0pp: 21%→12%)，\n      因 RE 的 zero-F1 问题 (48.5%) 不受 LoRA rank 影响——\n      这是 task difficulty 驱动的 fundamental limitation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 11: LoRA Rank Ablation — SciERC NER (N=8, T=1.0, n=529)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"rank_16_baseline\", \"rank_8\", \"Delta\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"greedy F1\", 0.664, 0.625, \"-3.9pp\"]\n          - [\"oracle F1\", 0.775, 0.812, \"+3.7pp\"]\n          - [\"oracle headroom\", \"10.85pp\", \"18.7pp\", \"+7.85pp\"]\n          - [\"degeneracy rate\", \"21.0%\", \"5.2%\", \"-15.8pp\"]\n          - [\"SJ rho\", 0.360, 0.378, \"+0.018\"]\n          - [\"FK rho\", 0.267, 0.288, \"+0.021\"]\n          - [\"LP rho\", 0.205, 0.252, \"+0.047\"]\n          - [\"VC rho\", 0.379, 0.408, \"+0.029\"]\n          - [\"LP selection gap vs greedy\", \"+0.6pp (p=0.39)\", \"+3.6pp (p=0.015)\", \"+3.0pp\"]\n          - [\"SJ selection gap vs greedy\", \"-1.9pp\", \"+2.8pp (p=0.042)\", \"+4.7pp\"]\n          - [\"LP range median (nats)\", 0.041, 0.074, \"+0.033\"]\n          - [\"tied fraction (F1)\", \"21.0%\", \"5.2%\", \"-15.8pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table 12: Degeneracy Drivers — Evidence Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"F1\", \"degen_pct\", \"driver\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CoNLL rank=16 5ep\", 0.912, 58, \"high capability + aggressive FT\"]\n          - [\"SciERC rank=16 5ep\", 0.664, 21, \"moderate capability + aggressive FT\"]\n          - [\"SciERC rank=8 5ep\", 0.625, 5.2, \"moderate capability + MILD FT\"]\n          - [\"Few-NERD rank=16 3ep\", 0.778, 5.4, \"high capability + MILD FT\"]\n          - [\"SciERC 4B rank=16 5ep\", 0.661, 10.4, \"lower capability + aggressive FT\"]\n          - [\"WNUT rank=16 5ep\", 0.523, 0, \"low capability (no convergence)\"]\n      - name: \"Table 13: QE vs Selection Decoupling\"\n        columns: [\"Config\", \"SJ_rho (QE)\", \"LP_sel_gap_pp (selection)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"rank=16\", 0.360, \"+0.6 (n.s.)\", \"good QE, no selection\"]\n          - [\"rank=8\", 0.378, \"+3.6 (p=0.015)\", \"good QE, good selection\"]\n          - [\"Delta\", \"+0.018\", \"+3.0pp\", \"QE stable, selection regime-dependent\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure 9 (CRITICAL): Paired bar chart — degeneracy rate and F1\n        side-by-side for rank=16 vs rank=8. Left bars (degeneracy): dramatic\n        drop 21%→5.2%. Right bars (F1): modest drop 0.664→0.625.\n        Annotated trade-off ratio: 4.05× degeneracy reduction per 1pp F1 cost.\n      - >\n        Figure 10: Dual-axis plot — LP within-instance range distributions\n        for rank=16 (compressed, peaked at 0.03-0.05) and rank=8\n        (wider, spread 0.04-0.12). Overlay: LP selection gap vs range bin\n        showing threshold effect (~0.06 nats needed for effective selection).\n      - >\n        Figure 11: Selection F1 vs N curves at rank=8, showing monotonic\n        improvement (LP: 0.625→0.640→0.652→0.661).\n        Contrast: rank=16 curves are flat (0.664→0.647→0.650→0.650).\n        Demonstrates recovered test-time scaling at lower LoRA rank.\n    analysis: >\n      LoRA rank=8 ablation 提供了 degeneracy causality 的最强证据。\n\n      (1) Fine-tuning intensity 是 degeneracy 的主驱动因素：\n      同一数据集、同一模型、同一 training data，仅改变 LoRA rank\n      就从 21% degeneracy 降至 5.2%。F1 仅下降 3.9pp。\n      这排除了 \"capability drives degeneracy\" 解释——\n      rank=8 的 NER capability 仍然很强 (F1=0.625)。\n\n      (2) Selection 从 \"fails\" 变为 \"works\"：同一 SciERC 数据，\n      rank=16 下 LP selection +0.6pp (n.s.)，rank=8 下 +3.6pp (p=0.015)。\n      Controlled experiment 证明 selection failure 是 regime-dependent。\n\n      (3) QE 与 selection 完全 decouple：SJ rho 0.360→0.378 (stable)，\n      LP selection gap 0.6→3.6pp (dramatic change)。\n      QE 是 signal 的 intrinsic property，不受 FT intensity 影响。\n      Selection 是 regime-dependent，受 degeneracy/compression 控制。\n\n      (4) Prescriptive implication：如果需要 multi-sample selection，\n      使用较低的 LoRA rank。Trade-off 量化：\n      每 1pp F1 cost 换取 4.05× degeneracy reduction。\n      在 SciERC 上，rank=8 + LP selection (0.661) vs\n      rank=16 greedy (0.664) = 仅 0.3pp 差距，\n      但获得了 uncertainty quantification 能力。\n\n      (5) 与 Few-NERD 证据互补：Few-NERD (3-epoch) 和 SciERC rank=8\n      都独立地表明 mild fine-tuning → low degeneracy → selection works。\n      两个独立 ablation 维度 (epoch × rank) 给出一致结论。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-019: Supervised Verifier (SKIPPED — hypothetical)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-019: simple_verifier_baseline (hypothetical)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-019\"\n    description: >\n      Supervised verifier baseline — SKIPPED per DDL constraint + scope creep risk.\n      以下为 hypothetical worst-tier predictions.\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"SKIPPED\"\n      skip_reason: \"DDL 10 days, scope creep risk, exp-016 LR ensemble already underperforms EM\"\n      hypothetical_if_run:\n        verifier_model: \"DeBERTa-v3-large\"\n        training_data: \"SciERC N=8 samples with F1 labels, 529*8=4232 instances\"\n        train_test_split: \"5-fold CV\"\n        ner_verifier_auroc: 0.828\n        ner_verifier_rho: 0.485\n        ner_verifier_selection_f1: 0.698\n        ner_oracle_gap_captured_pct: 24.1\n        ner_verifier_vs_best_unsupervised_auroc_delta: 0.079\n        ner_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 3.4\n        re_verifier_auroc: 0.782\n        re_verifier_selection_f1: 0.448\n        re_oracle_gap_captured_pct: 19.3\n        re_verifier_vs_greedy_pp: 2.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      [HYPOTHETICAL — NOT EXECUTED]\n      如果执行，supervised verifier 应能部分关闭 selection gap。\n      DeBERTa-v3-large 可以从 (input, output) pair 中学到\n      quality patterns：entity boundary correctness、\n      relation consistency with context、output completeness。\n      这些是 unsupervised signals 无法捕获的 learned features。\n\n      NER AUROC 0.828 (vs unsupervised best EM 0.749, +7.9pp) 证明\n      supervised 上界显著高于 unsupervised。\n      Selection F1 0.698 captures 24.1% oracle gap\n      (vs unsupervised LP ~0.5% at rank=16)。\n      这证明 information exists in the outputs，\n      但 unsupervised signals 无法 access it。\n\n      在 worst tier context 下，exp-019 的 hypothetical 结果\n      与 exp-023 (LoRA rank=8) 互补：\n      路径 A: 降低 FT intensity 保留输出多样性 → unsupervised selection works\n      路径 B: 训练 supervised verifier → learned selection works even on converged outputs\n      两条路径都证明 selection gap is closable，不是 fundamental impossibility。\n\n      SKIPPED 是正确决策——exp-023 已提供了更 elegant 的 actionable answer\n      (改 training config vs 训练额外 model)，且 scope 更 clean。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-019 SKIPPED。Hypothetical 结果支持 Future Work：\n      \"Two paths close the selection gap: (1) reducing fine-tuning intensity\n      restores unsupervised selection (exp-023), (2) trained verifiers\n      capture quality patterns inaccessible to unsupervised signals.\"\n      在 worst tier paper 中，exp-023 的 prescriptive finding\n      比 exp-019 的 supervised finding 更有 practical value——\n      不需要额外 labeled data 或 additional model。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-017: LLaMA on CoNLL (REGISTRY COMPLETE — worst-tier reinterpretation)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-017: ner_llama_conll (reinterpretation)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-017\"\n    description: >\n      LLaMA-3.1-8B on CoNLL-2003.\n      Registry 已有完整数据 (exp_017_llama_conll_infer).\n      此处提供 worst-tier 叙事重解读.\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"DONE_IN_REGISTRY\"\n      registry_ref: \"exp_017_llama_conll_infer\"\n      actual_metrics:\n        sj_rho_full: 0.4314\n        fk_rho_full: 0.4277\n        lp_rho_full: 0.3072\n        greedy_f1: 0.9266\n        oracle_headroom: 0.0177\n      worst_tier_reinterpretation: >\n        LLaMA CoNLL SJ rho=0.431 matches Qwen CoNLL rho=0.436.\n        Cross-model consistency 强，但在 worst tier 下这同时意味着\n        degeneracy pattern (high F1 → high degeneracy) 也跨模型一致——\n        不是 Qwen-specific artifact 而是 5-epoch LoRA fine-tuning 的通用效应。\n        如果对 LLaMA 也做 rank=8 ablation，预期同样会看到 degeneracy 大幅下降。\n    result_rationale: >\n      已完成实验，不需要 prediction。在 worst tier 下重新解读：\n      LLaMA 复现了 Qwen 的 CoNLL pattern (greedy_f1=0.927, 高 degeneracy,\n      selection 无效, oracle headroom 仅 1.77pp)。\n      这原本被解释为 \"capability trap is model-agnostic\"，\n      但现在应解释为 \"aggressive fine-tuning (5 epochs, rank=32 for LLaMA)\n      consistently produces high degeneracy regardless of model architecture.\"\n      Cross-model validation 的含义从 \"capability trap is universal\" 变为\n      \"fine-tuning-induced convergence is universal.\" 证据相同，解释不同。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      exp-017 无需新实验。Worst tier 仅改变解释框架：\n      LLaMA+CoNLL 的 high degeneracy 归因于 fine-tuning regime\n      而非 model capability。Cross-model consistency 反而 strengthens\n      worst tier 论点——两个不同架构 (Qwen3, LLaMA-3.1) 在相同\n      fine-tuning 强度下产生相同的 convergence pattern。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # exp-024: Claim Audit\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"exp-024: claim_audit\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-024\"\n    description: >\n      Systematic cross-chapter numerical consistency audit.\n      在 worst tier 下检查所有 claims 与新实验数据的一致性,\n      识别需要 rewrite 的 sections.\n    expected_results:\n      total_inconsistencies_found: 8\n      critical: 5\n      moderate: 2\n      minor: 1\n      critical_inconsistencies:\n        - id: \"CA-1\"\n          location: \"Abstract + Introduction\"\n          current_claim: \"'universally fail to select better candidates'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"Few-NERD LP +3.2pp (p=0.028); rank=8 LP +3.6pp (p=0.015)\"\n          fix: \"'fail to select under high-convergence regimes; succeed when output diversity is preserved'\"\n        - id: \"CA-2\"\n          location: \"Discussion line 3 vs Limitations line 8\"\n          current_claim: \"'+0.1pp over single-sample' vs '+0.4pp over greedy'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"exp_016_rerun_1024: LP selection +0.6pp (n.s., p=0.39)\"\n          fix: \"unify to '+0.6pp, not significant (bootstrap p=0.39, CI [-0.030, +0.042])'\"\n        - id: \"CA-3\"\n          location: \"Section 4.4 Capability Trap\"\n          current_claim: \"'structural inevitability: the better the model, the less TTS helps'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"R2=0.51 (4 datasets); rank=8 F1=0.625 with degen=5.2%\"\n          fix: \"'one factor among several; fine-tuning intensity is the primary driver of degeneracy'\"\n        - id: \"CA-4\"\n          location: \"Claim 1 PRIMARY\"\n          current_claim: \"'diagnose two failure mechanisms and a unifying capability trap'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"Few-NERD + rank=8 break capability trap; provide positive selection examples\"\n          fix: \"'diagnose conditions under which each mechanism activates; convergence drivers include FT intensity, entity density, task complexity'\"\n        - id: \"CA-5\"\n          location: \"Story Spine headline\"\n          current_claim: \"'T=0 greedy dominates all multi-sample strategies at zero cost'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"Few-NERD: LP +3.2pp > greedy (p=0.028); rank=8: LP +3.6pp > greedy (p=0.015)\"\n          fix: \"'T=0 greedy dominates under standard fine-tuning regimes, but multi-sample LP selection recovers 3-4pp when output diversity is preserved'\"\n      moderate_inconsistencies:\n        - id: \"CA-6\"\n          location: \"Scale ablation (4B)\"\n          current_claim: \"'4B degeneracy 10.4% supports capability trap'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"rank=8 provides alternative explanation (FT intensity, not capability)\"\n          fix: \"acknowledge confound: 4B lower degeneracy may reflect both reduced capability AND different convergence dynamics\"\n        - id: \"CA-7\"\n          location: \"SJ claims throughout\"\n          current_claim: \"'SJ clearly beats LP on NER (rho +0.15-0.22)'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"3-seed Fisher p=0.085 (borderline); seed 789 gap only 0.057\"\n          fix: \"soften to 'SJ tends to outperform LP on NER (p=0.085); VC>LP is more robust (p=0.018)'\"\n      minor_inconsistencies:\n        - id: \"CA-8\"\n          location: \"Figure 4 caption\"\n          current_claim: \"'monotonic relationship between F1 and degeneracy'\"\n          contradicting_evidence: \"R2=0.51 with Few-NERD, R2=0.35 with rank=8 data point\"\n          fix: \"update caption to reflect weak-to-moderate relationship\"\n      # Narrative restructuring\n      narrative_changes:\n        old_title: \"Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors: Why Confidence Signals Cannot Scale Structured Information Extraction\"\n        new_title: \"When Does Multi-Sample Selection Help Structured IE? A Diagnostic Study of Output Convergence\"\n        old_primary_claim: \"universal failure + capability trap as unifying framework\"\n        new_primary_claim: \"conditional effectiveness: selection fails under high-convergence regimes, succeeds with output diversity\"\n        old_paper_type: \"novel insight (negative result) paper\"\n        new_paper_type: \"large-scale empirical study with prescriptive guidelines\"\n        sections_requiring_major_rewrite:\n          - \"Abstract (remove 'universally', add conditions, mention positive Few-NERD/rank=8 results)\"\n          - \"Introduction (reframe as conditional study, not universal negative)\"\n          - \"Section 4.4 retitle: 'Output Convergence Drivers' (not 'Capability Trap')\"\n          - \"New Section 4.5: 'When Does Selection Succeed? — Prescriptive Guidelines'\"\n          - \"Discussion (trade-off analysis: F1 cost vs selection gain; practical recommendations)\"\n          - \"Conclusion (actionable takeaways for practitioners)\"\n        sections_minor_edits:\n          - \"Section 3 (add Few-NERD dataset description)\"\n          - \"Section 4.1 (add Few-NERD QE results)\"\n          - \"Section 4.2 (add Few-NERD selection results)\"\n          - \"Section 4.3 (add rank=8 ablation subsection)\"\n          - \"Related Work (reframe positioning vs TTS scaling literature)\"\n      # Capability trap degradation\n      capability_trap_r2_progression:\n        three_datasets: 0.98\n        four_datasets_with_fewnerd: 0.51\n        five_points_with_rank8: 0.35\n      # Prescriptive guidelines (new section content)\n      prescriptive_guidelines:\n        - condition: \"degeneracy < 10% AND LP range > 0.07 nats\"\n          recommendation: \"use LP-based best-of-N selection (expected gain 2-4pp)\"\n          evidence: \"Few-NERD (+3.2pp), rank=8 SciERC (+3.6pp)\"\n        - condition: \"degeneracy > 20%\"\n          recommendation: \"use T=0 greedy (zero additional cost)\"\n          evidence: \"SciERC rank=16 (+0.6pp n.s.), CoNLL (-1.0pp)\"\n        - condition: \"10% < degeneracy < 20%\"\n          recommendation: \"evaluate on dev set; marginal expected gain\"\n          evidence: \"borderline regime, outcome depends on specific dataset\"\n        - condition: \"RE with >40% zero-F1 instances\"\n          recommendation: \"no unsupervised signal reliably helps; consider supervised verifier\"\n          evidence: \"RE rankings unstable across all seeds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Claim audit 在 worst tier 下揭示 8 处不一致，其中 5 处 critical。\n      核心问题：现有文本围绕 \"universal failure + capability trap\" 构建，\n      但 Few-NERD 和 LoRA rank=8 直接推翻了 universality 和\n      structural inevitability。\n\n      CA-1 是最高优先级：Abstract 的 \"universally fail\" 被两个\n      statistically significant 正结果 (p=0.028, p=0.015) 直接否定。\n      如果保留 \"universally fail\"，reviewer 会立即指出与\n      Results section 的 internal contradiction。\n\n      CA-2 是 legacy 不一致，需要统一数字。\n\n      CA-3 是叙事核心变化：capability trap 从 unifying framework\n      降级为 one-of-several factors。R²=0.51 (4 datasets) 和 0.35 (5 points)\n      说明 F1 只解释 35-51% 的 degeneracy 方差。\n\n      CA-4 需要重构 Claim 1 从 \"why selection fails\" 到\n      \"when selection fails/succeeds and what drives the boundary\"。\n\n      CA-5 headline 变化反映从 pure negative 到 conditional finding。\n\n      Prescriptive guidelines 是 worst tier 最大的新贡献——\n      给 practitioners 具体的 decision criteria：\n      观察 degeneracy rate 和 LP range，决定是否使用 multi-sample 策略。\n      这比 \"selection always fails\" 有更大的 practical value。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A1: Claim Audit Summary\"\n        columns: [\"ID\", \"Severity\", \"Location\", \"Issue\", \"Fix\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CA-1\", \"CRITICAL\", \"Abstract\", \"universally fail vs 2 positive results\", \"add conditions\"]\n          - [\"CA-2\", \"CRITICAL\", \"Disc/Lim\", \"+0.1pp vs +0.4pp vs actual +0.6pp\", \"unify numbers\"]\n          - [\"CA-3\", \"CRITICAL\", \"Sec 4.4\", \"structural inevitability vs R2=0.51\", \"reframe as one factor\"]\n          - [\"CA-4\", \"CRITICAL\", \"Claim 1\", \"universal failure framing\", \"conditional framing\"]\n          - [\"CA-5\", \"CRITICAL\", \"Headline\", \"greedy dominates all vs 2 exceptions\", \"add regime qualifier\"]\n          - [\"CA-6\", \"MODERATE\", \"4B section\", \"4B degen interpretation confound\", \"acknowledge\"]\n          - [\"CA-7\", \"MODERATE\", \"SJ claims\", \"SJ>LP p=0.085 borderline\", \"soften claim\"]\n          - [\"CA-8\", \"MINOR\", \"Fig 4 cap\", \"monotonic claim vs R2=0.51\", \"update\"]\n      - name: \"Table A2: Prescriptive Decision Matrix\"\n        columns: [\"Degeneracy\", \"LP_Range_nats\", \"Recommendation\", \"Expected_Gain_pp\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"< 10%\", \"> 0.07\", \"LP best-of-N\", \"2-4\"]\n          - [\"10-20%\", \"0.04-0.07\", \"Evaluate on dev\", \"0-2\"]\n          - [\"> 20%\", \"< 0.04\", \"T=0 greedy\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"any (RE >40% zero-F1)\", \"any\", \"Supervised verifier or greedy\", \"0 unsupervised\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Figure S-audit: Capability trap R2 degradation bar chart.\n        3 bars: R2=0.98 (3 datasets), 0.51 (+ Few-NERD), 0.35 (+ rank=8).\n        Annotated: which data point caused each drop. Shows progressive\n        dissolution of the capability trap as evidence accumulates.\n    analysis: >\n      Claim audit 输出一个 comprehensive rewrite checklist。\n      核心变化不是 patch individual numbers——是叙事重构。\n\n      好消息：所有已有实验数据（free-form ablation、scale ablation、\n      cross-model validation、temperature analysis）不受影响。\n      它们仍然是 valid empirical contributions。\n      转向只需要重新 frame 这些数据的 interpretation。\n\n      Free-form ablation 仍证明 LP compression is model-intrinsic\n      (在 high-convergence regime 下)。Scale ablation 仍证明\n      cross-scale consistency。Cross-model 仍证明\n      cross-architecture generalization。\n\n      新 framing 有更清晰的层次：\n      Layer 1 (QE): confidence signals reliably estimate quality — robust across regimes.\n      Layer 2 (Selection): selection effectiveness depends on output convergence.\n      Layer 3 (Convergence drivers): FT intensity > entity density > task complexity > capability.\n      Layer 4 (Guidelines): prescriptive decision matrix for practitioners.\n\n      从 \"interesting negative finding\" 升级为 \"prescriptive empirical study\"，\n      对 EMNLP Main Conference fit 可能反而更好——\n      actionable findings 比 pure diagnostics 更 impactful。\n\n      Title 变更 essential：\n      \"Strong Predictors, Weak Selectors\" → \"When Does Multi-Sample Selection Help\"\n      反映从 universal negative 到 conditional study 的根本转向。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":39245,"cache_read_input_tokens":79110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":39245},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6745f76e-d74d-4b80-8f31-9d576877709a","uuid":"bd720145-787c-4bff-9af2-7c91f990bf10"}
